title: SAP ASE (Sybase): Errorlog
agents: linux
catalog: app/sybase
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check counts the lines of the SAP ASE (Sybase) errorlog that match an
 error pattern within a time window (default: {error:|error } within the last
 24 hours), reported by the agent plug-in {check_sybase}. Pattern, time window
 and path are configured in {/etc/check_mk/check_sybase.cfg}.

 Levels for the number of errors (default: CRIT from the first error) and the
 state if the errorlog is not readable (default: WARN) can be configured via
 the rule "SAP ASE (Sybase) Errorlog". The latest matching lines are shown in
 the service details.

item:
 The SID of the ASE instance.

discovery:
 One service is created for each instance with the errorlog check enabled.
